Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||09-12-2001||02:08 PM||||The White-Blue should be easy... but you need your front white layer to be partially transparent.  The Yellow to white- I don't think that'll work too easily.  You could turn it to green by putting blue behind it, or red by putting magenta behind it, etc...<P>Read this thread...the concept is the similiar.<BR><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010075.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010075.html</A><P>Email me about the TransWhite material if you're interested.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
